+    // --- atomics and barriers ---------------------------------------------
+    // The larx/stcx. family. The sub-word forms are ISA 2.07, which is
+    // POWER8, which is this port's floor: GNU as accepts lbarx/lharx/stbcx./
+    // sthcx. from -mpower8 and rejects them at -mpower7, and gcc at
+    // -mcpu=power7 falls back to a twenty-instruction masked lwarx word loop.
+    // So there is no hasISA30() gate here and nothing to test twice -- both
+    // generations execute identical code. See powerpc64le-handbook
+    // jsc-ppc64le-atomics-cas.md section 2.3 for the assembler gate and the
+    // encodings, which were checked against objdump before they were written.
+    //
+    // Every larx below encodes EH = 0, the "fetch and operate" hint, which is
+    // what Atomics.* on a shared typed array is and what gcc and clang emit
+    // for every __atomic builtin; EH = 1 is the lock-acquisition hint.
+    void lbarx(RegisterID rt, RegisterID ra, RegisterID rb) { insn(formX(31, rt, ra, rb, 52, false)); }
